<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 210)</h2>
<p><b>The watcher now runs overnight, with nobody's Mac open.</b></p>
<ul>
<li><code>Asobi watch --folder /renders/inbox --session ~/dailies/today.otio</code> runs headless — schedule it with launchd or from your pipeline's cron jobs.</li>
<li>Same rules as watching in the app: deliveries ingest only when <b>finished</b> (done-marker or write-quiescence), versions group under their shot, and what's already in the folder stays put.</li>
<li>Every finished delivery is appended to the session file <b>atomically</b> — an interruption never corrupts it. One log line per ingest.</li>
<li>Open the session in the morning: the review list built itself.</li>
</ul>
<p>Also: the first delivery into an empty session now loads on arrival — and later arrivals never yank the playhead mid-review.</p>
]]></description>
